<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prophet Muhammad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Prophet Muhammad was the founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, who lived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a> in the late sixth and early seventh centuries and died in 632 CE. His death without a designated successor led to the establishment of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a>, from which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> later emerged. Later Muslim states, from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>, drew legitimacy from descent from him or emulation of his example.</p></div>
